.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt EXIT 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm exit
.Nd terminate the calling process and all of its threads
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ft void
.Fn exit "int code"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
system call terminates the calling process and every thread it owns:
.Fa code
is stored for
.Xr proc_wait 2 ,
threads blocked in syscalls exit at their next scheduling point instead of returning to user
mode, scheme names and pending requests of the process are released, and its address space and
handle table are torn down once.
.Pp
A thread that must terminate only itself uses
.Xr thread_exit 2 .
An authorized caller can terminate another process with
.Xr proc_terminate 2 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn exit
does not return.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr proc_wait 2 ,
.Xr proc_terminate 2 ,
.Xr thread_exit 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
